---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/docs/CodeBlock.astro";

const toc = [
  { id: "diagnostics", label: "Collecting diagnostics" },
  { id: "common", label: "Common problems" },
  { id: "reporting", label: "Reporting a bug" },
];
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Troubleshooting"
  description="Diagnose failed scans, missing findings, and environment problems."
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: "Troubleshooting" }]}
  toc={toc}
>
  <h2 id="diagnostics">Collecting diagnostics</h2>
  <CodeBlock title="shell">aegis doctor
aegis scan --verbose --log-file aegis.log</CodeBlock>
  <p>
    <code>--verbose</code> writes the analysis plan, the generated tests, and
    every test result. Logs redact values that match the <code>secrets</code>
    rule pack.
  </p>

  <h2 id="common">Common problems</h2>
  <h3>"not a git repository"</h3>
  <p>
    Run Aegis from inside the working tree, or pass an explicit path:
    <code>aegis scan /path/to/repo</code>.
  </p>

  <h3>"base revision not found" during a diff scan</h3>
  <p>
    Your CI checkout is shallow. Fetch full history — with
    <code>actions/checkout@v4</code>, set <code>fetch-depth: 0</code>.
  </p>

  <h3>Exit status 4: the application under test never started</h3>
  <p>
    Set <code>tests.command</code> in <code>aegis.yml</code> to the command
    that starts your service, and confirm it works on its own. Increase
    <code>tests.timeout</code> for services with a slow boot.
  </p>

  <h3>A known issue is not reported</h3>
  <p>
    Verified reporting hides candidates that could not be reproduced. Re-run
    with <code>--include-unverified</code> to see them, and check that the file
    is not excluded by <code>scan.exclude</code> or an inline suppression.
  </p>

  <h3>Scans are slow</h3>
  <p>
    Scope the scan to a diff, raise <code>scan.concurrency</code>, and cache
    <code>~/.cache/aegis</code> in CI. Disabling
    <code>tests.enabled</code> makes scans faster, at the cost of verification.
  </p>

  <h2 id="reporting">Reporting a bug</h2>
  <p>
    Open an issue with the output of <code>aegis --version</code> and
    <code>aegis doctor</code>, the command you ran, and the relevant portion
    of the verbose log.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="https://github.com/denny200897/SITCON-hacker-zone/issues">Issue tracker</a></li>
    <li><a href="https://github.com/denny200897/SITCON-hacker-zone/security">Security policy</a> — report vulnerabilities in Aegis privately.</li>
  </ul>
</DocsLayout>
